drawFieldsT -- the drawing fields and the form attributes at the top of Topics/forms (the forms incantation), which
incant/utilities loads. SEQ 629, 2026-11-12; virtual since SEQ 630 and SEQ 631, the same day.

DF-1  FORMs holds the 35 drawing fields, the 28 form attributes, the 7 unparked drawing entries (PoinT, ArC and the five
      perforation templates; CurvE the rule is a second mention of CurvE the field) and the three defined here (73).
      (utilities loads Topics/forms; including it here as well would define every field twice.)
DF-2  LinE carries its Core Graphics function and signature, once; X is there.
DF-3  every field in FORMs that forms write is virtual, so each write is the writing field's own copy: width 100 and
      300, and WidtH 100 and 300 (before SEQ 631 WidtH was not virtual and both read 300, the last write). The control
      is dfShared, defined here and not virtual: three fields write 100, 200 and 300 and all read 300.
DF-4  the registry's own width, fill and WidtH print with no value after those writes.
DF-5  THE UNPARKED TEMPLATES (Tony, 2026-11-12). A template lists one field several times with different values, and
      before virtual every one of those writes landed in the one definition. Now PerfRighT prints
      DowN=GaP LefT=DeptH DowN=StridE RighT=DeptH: its two DowN are two copies. PerforatioN's PerfLefT=5 is its own
      copy too, holding 5, and the registry's PerfLefT keeps no value and its four entries.
      PoinT, ArC and CurvE are defined as rule shapes only. PoinT's old action is not carried: it is written in the
      old drawing spellings (its text: git ede70292^, IncantForms/WorkingOn/drawing).
